        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#FFF9E6;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=11;" value="Notes:&lt;br&gt;• USER covers Student, Lecturer and Administrator (via ROLE) and keeps the person&#39;s details (name, username, student/lecturer code, class). Each user has exactly one USER ACCOUNT with the sign-in data: account name, email, Google link, salt + password hash (never the plain password). A user signs in with Google (if linked) and/or with account name or email + password (if set).&lt;br&gt;• INTERVIEW TURN = one question (main or follow-up) + the student&#39;s answer transcript; the audio file is kept in Object Storage.&lt;br&gt;• RUBRIC = the scoring guide of one question, made of RUBRIC CRITERION items (description + max points). The AI gives each criterion a CRITERION SCORE; their sum is the AI-suggested score kept on QUESTION RESPONSE with the AI feedback.&lt;br&gt;• SCORE REVIEW = the lecturer&#39;s final score for the attempt (pending until the lecturer confirms it); it starts at the sum of the AI-suggested scores.&lt;br&gt;• EMAIL LINK TOKEN = one-time, expiring email link: verify the email after registering, set the account name and password (account-setup link), or reset a forgotten password (reset link: password only).&lt;br&gt;• AI SERVICE CONFIG = STT/TTS/LLM provider, endpoint, encrypted API key and STT/TTS language (VI/EN).&lt;br&gt;• A draft EXAM SESSION may have no questions yet, and a QUESTION may have no rubric yet. It can be published only when it has at least one question, every question has a rubric and at least one student is on the list.&lt;br&gt;• PARTICIPANT = a student on the session&#39;s list, imported by the lecturer. Only listed students can start an attempt, one attempt each, inside the session time window.&lt;br&gt;• A question not reached before the session closes has no QUESTION RESPONSE; it counts as 0 in the attempt total." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="700" width="860" height="215" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
